From: lfdevs <lfdevs@lfdevs.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 00:40:35 +0800
Subject: backend-anland: handle extended input and runtime refresh

Consume every message arriving on the Anland data socket so unknown
frames cannot leave the Weston event loop spinning on unread data. Bound
partial message waits, drain variable-length clipboard and text payloads,
and receive then close unsupported resource descriptors.

Handle live display refresh events by updating the Weston output mode
and repaint cadence. Recognize the remaining Anland 5.13 input types,
reject malformed framing, and move the transport back to fallback when
an expected payload or descriptor message does not arrive.
---
